It's an interesting tradeoff between having good AC and having nifty
armor. I've found for my high conduct games, that my AC gets worse
throughout the game.

For example, in the middle game I might have:
+1 dwarvish mithril
+2 rusty iron shoes
+3 burnt leather helm
+3 burnt small shield,it's not too uncommon to find a valkyrie bones
file :)
+2 gloves
+1 robe
For an AC = -12

But then piece by piece I start replacing those high AC items with
magic armor without bonuses:
+0 Dragon scales
+0 burnt jumping boots
+1 robe (or perhaps +0 displacement)
+0 gauntlets of power (depending on spinach availability)
+3 thoroughly burnt leather helm
+0 silver shield
For an AC = -2 (or there abouts is typical for me, sometimes more,
sometimes less)


